{
 "encounter_id": "00774",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello, doctor. It's the whiplash, from the car crash in the summer. I'm better but not right, if you know what I mean."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tell me how it is now."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My neck's stiff, especially in the mornings, and I get a pain across my shoulders by the afternoon. Worse after driving."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long is it since the accident? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Four months. It was better at two months, then it plateaued. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is the pain going down your arms, any numbness or tingling?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing in my arms. No tingling."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What are you using for the pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Naproxen, 250 mg, twice a day, maybe? And paracetamol, 1 gram, but I only take that when it's bad, so not every day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. So 250 mg twice a day, as you recall it, and the paracetamol only when it's bad. Remind me of your history."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High blood pressure, a stomach ulcer, years ago, and my back's not great. Slipped disc."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you had any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "An operation on my lower back, a discectomy, in 2014."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Are you working?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, I'm a delivery driver. Hours in the van."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me look at your neck. Sit on the couch. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Tender over the muscles on both sides of the neck, tight and knotted in the upper shoulder muscles, and the movement is limited when you look over your shoulder."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that normal for four months on? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's common. Whiplash can take months to settle, and the muscles tighten and guard. I'd say this is a persisting whiplash strain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Will it ever clear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Most people recover, usually by six months, but you need to keep the neck moving. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've been scared to. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I understand. Gentle exercises and physiotherapy help most. I'd like to arrange a referral for physio."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "A few weeks. Meanwhile, I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the neck, to be thorough, given the time that's passed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Also, naproxen and your old stomach ulcer don't mix well, so please always take it with food."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've been taking it on an empty stomach, I'll stop. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Take it only with food, and if you get stomach pain, or black stools, stop it and ring us. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Thank you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Use a warm pack, and break up your driving with stops to stretch."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If the pain spreads into your arm, or you get weakness or numbness in your hands, come back that day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I will. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
